            {
              "type": "ai_overview",
              "rank_group": 1,
              "rank_absolute": 6,
              "page": 1,
              "position": "left",
              "xpath": "/html[1]/body[1]/div[3]/div[1]/div[15]/div[1]/div[2]/div[2]/div[1]/div[1]/div[3]/div[8]/div[1]/div[1]",
              "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
              "markdown": "Insider buying is the legal purchase of a company's shares by its own executives, directors, or major shareholders (owning 10% or more) using public information.[[1]](https://www.sec.gov/data-research/sec-markets-data/insider-transactions-data-sets)[[2]](https://www.investopedia.com/terms/i/insider-buying.asp)\n\n- **SEC Form 4:** Insiders must report their open-market stock purchases and sales to the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) within **two business days** of the transaction.[[1]](https://www.quiverquant.com/insiders/)[[2]](https://www.sec.gov/data-research/sec-markets-data/insider-transactions-data-sets)\n- **Legality vs. Illegal Insider Trading:** Insider *buying* is completely legal when it relies on public information or standard compensation. Illegal insider trading occurs when anyone trades securities while possessing material, non-public information in breach of a fiduciary duty.[[1]](https://www.investopedia.com/terms/i/insider-buying.asp)[[2]](https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/glossary/insider-trading)\n\n### Why Investors Track Insider Buying\n\n- **Confidence Signal:** Executives typically buy shares because they believe the stock is undervalued or that future performance will improve . As the saying goes, insiders might sell stock for many reasons (such as personal diversification or liquidity), but they usually buy for only one: they expect the price to go up.[[1]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TjfUiA_fU4A)[[2]](https://www.investopedia.com/terms/i/insider-buying.asp)\n- **Cluster Buys:** Investors often look for \"cluster purchases,\" which happen when multiple executives or board members buy shares of the same company around the same time.[[1]](https://www.insiderscreener.com/en/)\n- **Limitations:** Public disclosures usually hit the database a day or two after the trade. Because the market often prices in these shifts quickly, retail investors rarely capture an immediate or guaranteed edge.[[1]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=daMWQTAPAeQ&t=48)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GcoTiTBrYMY&t=143)\n\n### Where to Track Live Insider Trades\n\n- [OpenInsider](http://openinsider.com/) : A free, searchable database for tracking recent SEC Form 4 insider filings.[[1]](http://openinsider.com/)\n- [Quiver Quantitative](https://www.quiverquant.com/insiders/) : An insider trading dashboard tracking executive buy-and-sell sentiment.[[1]](https://www.quiverquant.com/insiders/)\n- [SEC Form 4](https://www.secform4.com/) : A tracker for real-time insider and institutional filings directly from SEC EDGAR.[[1]](https://www.secform4.com/)",
